Sorry, I should have clarified what the "bits_of_evidence" values was.
It is not a p-value. It is a likelihood ratio. See Glover & Dixon
(2004, www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15732688 <http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15732688>) and Johannson (2011,
www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21077903 <http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/21077903>) for a description of likelihood
ratios.

